<div id="S4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Metrics:</span>
The evaluation of the 2D detection models is based on the widely used  <a href="#id4"><span href="#id4" title="CrowdQuery: Density-Guided Query Module for Enhanced 2D and 3D Detection in Crowded Scenes" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">AP</span></a> (<a href="#id4"><abbr href="#id4" title="CrowdQuery: Density-Guided Query Module for Enhanced 2D and 3D Detection in Crowded Scenes" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">AP</abbr></a>) and Miss Rate (MR<sup id="S4.SS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_sup">-2</sup>) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For 3D evaluation, we use the metrics presented by STCrowd <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>.
First, the  <a href="#id5"><span href="#id5" title="CrowdQuery: Density-Guided Query Module for Enhanced 2D and 3D Detection in Crowded Scenes" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">mAP</span></a> (<a href="#id5"><abbr href="#id5" title="CrowdQuery: Density-Guided Query Module for Enhanced 2D and 3D Detection in Crowded Scenes" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">mAP</abbr></a>), based on the <a href="#id4"><abbr href="#id4" title="CrowdQuery: Density-Guided Query Module for Enhanced 2D and 3D Detection in Crowded Scenes" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">AP</abbr></a> definition of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>, is employed.
The 3D center distance serves as the matching criterion.
Three different distance thresholds <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=\{0.25,0.5,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.25</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\{0.25,0.5,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> are used and averaged to calculate the final <a href="#id5"><abbr href="#id5" title="CrowdQuery: Density-Guided Query Module for Enhanced 2D and 3D Detection in Crowded Scenes" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">mAP</abbr></a>.
Second, the  <a href="#id6"><span href="#id6" title="CrowdQuery: Density-Guided Query Module for Enhanced 2D and 3D Detection in Crowded Scenes" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">AR</span></a> (<a href="#id6"><abbr href="#id6" title="CrowdQuery: Density-Guided Query Module for Enhanced 2D and 3D Detection in Crowded Scenes" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">AR</abbr></a>) metric is introduced, which captures the model’s recall performance for different occlusion levels.
The <a href="#id6"><abbr href="#id6" title="CrowdQuery: Density-Guided Query Module for Enhanced 2D and 3D Detection in Crowded Scenes" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">AR</abbr></a> is calculated for the occlusion labels 0 (no occlusion), 1 (no more than half the body), and 2 (over half the body).
For occlusion label <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> the <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AR_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AR_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is determined by:</p>
<table id="S4.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AR_{i}=\frac{1}{|D|}\sum_{d\in D}Recall_{i,d},i\in\{0,1,2\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AR_{i}=\frac{1}{|D|}\sum_{d\in D}Recall_{i,d},i\in\{0,1,2\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">TABLE III</span>: </span><span id="S4.T3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Impact of Density guidance on 3D Object Detection tested on STCrowd. The notations @1 and @3 indicate in which decoder layer the density cross-attention is utilized.</span></figcaption>
